  "scope": "Core inspect_group_recovery composes complete stored-member graph, short-circuit completion, required chain and sequence proofs, native state decoding, state/receipt admission and final native records in the original SQLite order. The reference adapter retains owner/plan admission, SQL, bounded decoding, exact original receipt correspondence, cold reservation/original-watermark checks and the outer recovery transaction. Eight real flow forms produce 22 group states and 374 frozen fault-order comparisons with every original metadata/effect/dispatch/group/member table unchanged. Independent core consumers cover 96 state/policy combinations, bounded graph refusal before native work, local opaque keys and receipts, original native error ownership, every reached callback unwind and late record/commit failure before checkpoint handoff with distinct native keys. Policy flags must derive from an already-admitted original plan/state, never untrusted requests to skip checks. The borrowed host owns one stable snapshot and bounds native work; receipts/errors move without Clone, Debug, serde or thread bounds. This adds no evaluator, dispatch, fuel, identity allocation, storage write or automatic rollback. Cross-group identity checks, authentic original grants/budgets and final commit before publishing a complete checkpoint remain external. This is a per-group recovery inspection, not a complete native durable VM, new wire schema or physical repository extraction.",
